\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Open comparison questions}
\tag{ftip}
\p{The matrix in \ref{ftip-00LZ} is a protocol map, not a result table. The
following probes keep the five capability coordinates separate and leave an
unknown cell visible until the required records exist. Each probe names its
source, estimand, controls, and evaluation coordinates so that a missing record
cannot be mistaken for a zero score.}

\ol{
  \li{\strong{State access.} Sources: [Mamba, Sections 3.1--3.3](https://arxiv.org/html/2312.00752v2#S3) and [linear attention, Sections 3.2--3.3](https://arxiv.org/html/2006.16236v3#S3). Estimand: the paired difference in retrieval utility and #{K_{\rm state}}. Controls: Transformer, Mamba, and linear-attention systems on a predeclared retrieval and continuation suite at matched parameter, context, recipe, and cost budgets. Evaluation: report cost, recurrence or summary stability, and state observability. Scope boundary: a long-context score does not transfer to another task family without its task and transport record.}
  \li{\strong{Recurrent feedback.} Source: [Recurrent Looped Transformer, Sections 2--3 and 5--8](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.07591). Estimand: the paired change in finite-task utility and #{K_{\rm state}} from decoder feedback. Controls: a common causal encoder, model size, training tokens, seeds, and matched per-token budget, with no-feedback and declared chunk-size arms. Evaluation: report recurrent-state bytes, encoder/decoder FLOPs, chunk latency, numerical/training stability, and feedback monitorability. Scope boundary: parity, permutation tracking, and modular arithmetic remain finite evidence; without a deployment and transfer record, the cell is finite-only.}
  \li{\strong{Residual rewrite.} Source: [Deep Delta Learning, Sections 2--4 and 6](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.00417). Estimand: the paired change in utility and rewrite-sensitive state behavior from a gated rank-one read/compare/target/write edit. Controls: residual capacity, optimizer, tokens, seeds, and model family, with no-write, write-only, and capacity-matched arms. Evaluation: report rewrite and residual-state monitorability, inference FLOPs, memory, numerical stability, and a held-out transfer task. Scope boundary: finite GPT-2 observations do not identify a general capability gain or architecture-wide law.}
  \li{\strong{Adaptive computation.} Source: [Continuous Thought Machine, Sections 3.1--3.5](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.05522v4#S3) and the looped-model contract in \ref{ftip-00KG}. Estimand: the paired change in utility and #{K_{\rm adapt}} per charged internal tick or loop. Controls: common input, base model, recipe, stopping rule, and charged internal compute. Evaluation: report tick/loop cost, training and inference stability, and stopping-signal monitorability. Scope boundary: an observed adaptive gain remains conditional on that stopping law.}
  \li{\strong{Representation and abstraction.} Sources: [I-JEPA, Section 3](https://arxiv.org/html/2301.08243v3#S3) and [SplitJEPA, Sections 3.1--3.4](https://arxiv.org/html/2610.12349v1#S3). Estimand: subspace identifiability and the conditional change in #{K_{\rm repr}}. Controls: fixed correspondences, full-rank variant differences, normalization, encoder budget, and matched downstream probes. Evaluation: report probe cost, optimization stability, and subspace monitorability. Scope boundary: the conditional subspace result is separate from downstream task transfer; failure of a premise is an incompatible cell, not a zero score.}
  \li{\strong{Plasticity.} Source: the objective and optimizer interfaces in \ref{ftip-00JM} and the I-JEPA intervention description in \ref{ftip-00OQ}. Estimand: the paired change in #{K_{\rm plast}} after a declared post-training intervention. Controls: common recipe and equal-tuning arms with data, optimizer, trial count, stopping, and feedback fixed or explicitly varied. Evaluation: report intervention cost, training stability, and update-signal monitorability. Scope boundary: an intervention effect is limited to the declared base artifact, task, and objective; it does not transfer across architectures without a new paired record.}
  \li{\strong{Portability.} Sources: the Mamba, BDH, and Neural Operator method descriptions in \ref{ftip-00OQ}: [Mamba](https://arxiv.org/html/2312.00752v2#S3), [BDH](https://arxiv.org/html/2509.26507v1#S3.SS2), and [Neural Operators](https://arxiv.org/html/2108.08481v6#S3). Estimand: survival of the declared utility and #{K_{\rm port}} across one transfer edge. Controls: source model, task family, model scale, deployment regime, evaluation law, and cost vector retained as paired fields. Evaluation: report migration cost, stability after the shift, and failure monitorability. Scope boundary: evidence for one transfer edge does not order unmeasured edges; blank edges remain unmeasured.}
  \li{\strong{Adjunct interactions.} Sources: [liquid time-constant networks, Sections 1--2](https://arxiv.org/html/2006.04439v4#S2), [Neural Operators, Section 3](https://arxiv.org/html/2108.08481v6#S3), and [I-JEPA, Section 3](https://arxiv.org/html/2301.08243v3#S3). Estimand: the joint change in the declared capability coordinates after an explicit intervention. Controls: declared core model, objective, temporal law, function-space bias, matched controls, and separate single-intervention arms. Evaluation: report joint and marginal costs, numerical/training stability, and interaction monitorability. Scope boundary: a joint effect is limited to the declared core, task, temporal law, and function-space regime; it does not transfer across regimes without separate intervention records.}
}

\p{These probes do not establish a common ordering of architecture families.
They specify what would count as evidence for a declared bottleneck change, while
cost, numerical stability, monitorability, and transfer remain separate
evaluation coordinates. Paired observations should use \ref{ftip-00L4}, the
study arms of \ref{ftip-00LS}, and the capability vector of \ref{ftip-00JM}.
Recurrent feedback and residual rewrite remain separate arms in every record;
a finite result without a deployment arm stays finite-only.}
